{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["And he said to them: Hear now, you rebels — just as this staff, which has almond blossoms, proves that it is — for a keep, for a sign against the children of rebellion." "Shall we bring forth for you water from this rock? — at the time of raising his hand with the staff — and he struck the rock twice — then he said to them in anger and wrath: Do you suppose that from this rock we shall bring forth water for you?! And Moshe said this out of uncertainty, for he erred regarding what the Holy One, blessed be He, had told him: Take the staff — and he did not believe that by speaking to the rock it would bring forth water from it, but rather by striking with the staff, as he had done at Rephidim. And what the Holy One, blessed be He, had told him: and you shall speak to the rock — he thought that this was the 'speaking to the rock' stated regarding the staff, and therefore he struck the rock twice, as it were in wrath and anger, and in doubt: if it brings forth water — well and good; and if not, I shall speak to the rock afterward. And the Holy One, blessed be He, agreed, through Moshe, that the water would come out by means of striking it; yet even so he was punished, for the Holy One, blessed be He, is exacting with the righteous — and this is what the Holy One, blessed be He, said: Because you did not believe in Me, to sanctify Me — by means of their speaking to the rock. Because He is exacting with the righteous even to a hair's breadth. And since I, the commentator, know that Moshe Rabbenu was nothing but inadvertent in transgressing the word of the Holy One, blessed be He, therefore I am obligated to explain that Moshe Rabbenu erred, as I have explained."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {0 "The comment appears to cite or allude to the language of Numbers 17:25, but Rashbam writes no citation; the syntax is terse and possibly elliptical."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community 